Z||000000||mikemrq||07-18-2001||10:33 AM||||had to remove the distributor, when i put it back it, i noticed that i have an oil leak at the base. should there be an 0-ring or a gasket on the shaft? there wasn't one when i removed it. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||07-18-2001||10:42 AM||||Yep - there's an O-ring that goes on there.  Available at (almost) any parts store.  If the O-ring is left off, you have an instant oil mess.  Pretty slick, huh   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ? <P>Edit:  Well... I <B>thought</B> most parts stores would carry the O-rings!  Then I read   Bluebottlejunky's post- apparently I was wrong.  Pretty sure I get mine at NAPA.  Anyway, call first and make sure they've got them, before you run off to your local parts purveyor.<P>Sorry I spoke too soon  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">   <p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 07-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Joe Torma||07-18-2001||10:42 AM||||You are correct...there should be an o-ring.<BR>I've had them go plenty.<P>Joe||||reg||1
